  "notes": {
    "uk|Passenger compensation": "UK flight-delay compensation is retained Regulation (EC) 261/2004, not an Act. Consumer Rights Act 2015 covers services generally.",
    "au-cth|Passenger compensation": "Australia has no EU261-style delay compensation; the 1959 Act covers carrier liability for death, injury and baggage, and the Australian Consumer Law covers services.",
    "sg|Consumer/tenancy": "Singapore has no residential tenancy Act; residential leases rest on contract and general property law. The strata Act is listed on SSO as the Building (Strata Management) Act 2004; the Building Maintenance and Strata Management title is superseded.",
    "au-vic|Termination/severance": "Victoria referred its industrial relations powers to the Commonwealth; unfair dismissal and redundancy are under the Fair Work Act 2009.",
    "au-wa|Customs/duties": "State 'duties' means stamp duty. Customs is a Commonwealth matter.",
    "uk|Leave/holiday pay": "Statutory holiday entitlement is in the Working Time Regulations 1998, a statutory instrument, not an Act.",
    "au-vic|Payroll/wages": "Wage Theft Act 2020 dropped: the Victorian register lists it only as made, with no in-force version, although a Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 exists. Worth checking by hand.",
    "nz|Insurance claims": "Contracts of Insurance Act 2024 is enacted but NOT YET IN FORCE. Kept deliberately: encoding a regime before it commences is the LQA use case. Until commencement, claims rest on the Insurance Law Reform Acts 1977 and 1985 and the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 (not verified here).",
    "au-nsw|Utility billing": "The Energy and Utilities Administration Act 1987 appears in the NSW in-force table under its former title, Energy Administration Act 1987."
